t }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | $(t-s){e}^{3t}$ |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334824/field-1" "q-334824/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334848/field-1/a123fb88e23c85655a143f2b55f8e7a00592e352769fa2b4e73c95c4fcfe463a" :answer/id #uuid "35ed53d0-c307-5afc-8796-62c65e3a9b0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e^{5(t-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334848/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "32036138-b4c0-5251-953d-08c1537c6ea8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334848/field-1/a123fb88e23c85655a143f2b55f8e7a00592e352769fa2b4e73c95c4fcfe463a" :answer-field/choices ["q-334848/field-1/a123fb88e23c85655a143f2b55f8e7a00592e352769fa2b4e73c95c4fcfe463a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334848/field-2/4549aae17f8c8103684e051f55b2d30deee83a112b49d939d0eea2f5c809b2be" :answer/id #uuid "4cd5b35e-88ec-5e28-8f15-1a1e200d4d99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334848/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd155588-c6a7-53b7-9369-4678074ffc3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334848/field-2/4549aae17f8c8103684e051f55b2d30deee83a112b49d939d0eea2f5c809b2be" :answer-field/choices ["q-334848/field-2/4549aae17f8c8103684e051f55b2d30deee83a112b49d939d0eea2f5c809b2be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334848" :question/id #uuid "b4a7f2ab-105a-5f1d-9c97-2c5083b74394" :question/math-academy-id "q-334848" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334848/field-1" "q-334848/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334848"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335054/field-1/fbadd866f3220b6ea004b8bb0a23775e5b50871cabd9d8da37a4923c39844c6f" :answer/id #uuid "f945c000-ab64-59b6-a625-ec622f6d5658" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335054/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a58cb1c-f7c0-59e6-9a36-eddaabe0bad3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335054/field-1/fbadd866f3220b6ea004b8bb0a23775e5b50871cabd9d8da37a4923c39844c6f" :answer-field/choices ["q-335054/field-1/fbadd866f3220b6ea004b8bb0a23775e5b50871cabd9d8da37a4923c39844c6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335054" :question/id #uuid "88a0cfc5-5a1e-5de6-b7ad-d22edba49f42" :question/math-academy-id "q-335054" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335054/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183/field-1/6998421d12249787a49c0d11d34aba1fce4f706f411ee2431c58829f994d5d8a" :answer/id #uuid "b4c239b4-9905-5857-b7b8-811115cbeeaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183/field-1/c46c107ab52561b188c0c5b83a2ad7662b5428bc1386c771be29e858c48722ef" :answer/id #uuid "de5f0019-4308-56d5-910e-fcb9c4e10689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183/field-1/6af3687036885c656f33bb039f5955d43d9ce18bcc9364f69deb05bac6cdd2c3" :answer/id #uuid "5e685ebb-21e3-503a-aace-3a7f5b586b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183/field-1/1520d475d8e743d03733ad83c320ba8cd758550512a3dd9459d034ca29edfca6" :answer/id #uuid "1ce90e4c-f672-50da-9c28-f1f286ab3c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f44f001-cfbe-58f5-8c39-afd3e99edb7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335183/field-1/c46c107ab52561b188c0c5b83a2ad7662b5428bc1386c771be29e858c48722ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-335183/field-1/6998421d12249787a49c0d11d34aba1fce4f706f411ee2431c58829f994d5d8a" "q-335183/field-1/c46c107ab52561b188c0c5b83a2ad7662b5428bc1386c771be29e858c48722ef" "q-335183/field-1/6af3687036885c656f33bb039f5955d43d9ce18bcc9364f69deb05bac6cdd2c3" "q-335183/field-1/1520d475d8e743d03733ad83c320ba8cd758550512a3dd9459d034ca29edfca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335183" :question/id #uuid "9ba8d18b-c5fe-5645-a494-a8fce82f879d" :question/math-academy-id "q-335183" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7x(t)+7,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335183/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335183"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335081/field-1/61d052124675aa6a88a9d359376119d727d1d522d12c8c4cea1f32ebd4aa6584" :answer/id #uuid "c839f570-293e-53e8-a790-fbcb91862b99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335081/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "da5f29b7-5278-579d-a488-0b572ea7ee86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-335081/field-1/61d052124675aa6a88a9d359376119d727d1d522d12c8c4cea1f32ebd4aa6584" :answer-field/choices ["q-335081/field-1/61d052124675aa6a88a9d359376119d727d1d522d12c8c4cea1f32ebd4aa6584"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335081" :question/id #uuid "6f5ce39d-f8ab-59ab-9317-85eea4eb36e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-335081" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335081/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335081"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334531/field-1/36ebbc0e332c702726138708c583505e1963c47a11c90518b2309bb8661fbc02" :answer/id #uuid "1ad39653-4f8f-5ccb-9769-cda7aa00b02d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334531/field-1/ab883208590419a2899663ef2b1ae25e7314de1c88347addc2f7fba67d725acf" :answer/id #uuid "351a60ca-4701-5d75-a1ce-f24582f45662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+3\\cos(2t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228135 :answer-field/correct "q-334531/field-1/36ebbc0e332c702726138708c583505e1963c47a11c90518b2309bb8661fbc02" :answer-field/choices ["q-334531/field-1/36ebbc0e332c702726138708c583505e1963c47a11c90518b2309bb8661fbc02" "q-334531/field-1/ab883208590419a2899663ef2b1ae25e7314de1c88347addc2f7fba67d725acf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334531"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127/field-1/6e5a73153d254c56abe40facd53e673543fd4d5bbdd337c0357f9fc06ba092c7" :answer/id #uuid "cd75eb09-0c02-503b-a42c-3ce6b51ab7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127/field-1/4a9e90b8a91a759ff42cb0993460d2b684fc9b57c50c9f218542c7be32a42162" :answer/id #uuid "502d0c3e-9dea-5669-ac81-6be30bc3f421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127/field-1/a4cb92f53b3718a7e44693fc79557399ee9e0fd3dee98b86a849783f48666aa2" :answer/id #uuid "3914c135-609a-55b3-8902-d92e6c1278e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127/field-1/1e24554c2ffd6628a07b95c0a96ffb434f2e711fc01668722b9798f5e576d414" :answer/id #uuid "453d92b8-de56-5a2b-a1b6-25ce6399d7a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "08a54479-a913-5967-a4c1-c58f1966973f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335127/field-1/1e24554c2ffd6628a07b95c0a96ffb434f2e711fc01668722b9798f5e576d414" :answer-field/choices ["q-335127/field-1/6e5a73153d254c56abe40facd53e673543fd4d5bbdd337c0357f9fc06ba092c7" "q-335127/field-1/4a9e90b8a91a759ff42cb0993460d2b684fc9b57c50c9f218542c7be32a42162" "q-335127/field-1/a4cb92f53b3718a7e44693fc79557399ee9e0fd3dee98b86a849783f48666aa2" "q-335127/field-1/1e24554c2ffd6628a07b95c0a96ffb434f2e711fc01668722b9798f5e576d414"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335127" :question/id #uuid "68df3c8f-765d-5e48-915e-50a1830db3e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335127" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n| $[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335127/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335401/field-1/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" :answer/id #uuid "251b661c-fbf4-56a6-827a-a0cbe273a45e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335401/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" :answer/id #uuid "f99fea25-2824-5456-a5bb-e5ff4e81399c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335401/field-1/90f9b3aa8bf944a7feca6948bc9b4f8b714976f2a4f40ee10776f871c3970cd2" :answer/id #uuid "745cb277-b798-5d1e-9293-0dc768a87e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335401/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" :answer/id #uuid "ff9290fe-71ca-5cc6-af0b-b3b5010dc72a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335401/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c0ebb87-d15a-56f3-bcac-452c516bb4cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335401/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" :answer-field/choices ["q-335401/field-1/0d652a7f8f9c1a42526cff8daf2a3a3ea56f579cc8a9cef8a5cb8d5922125a76" "q-335401/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" "q-335401/field-1/90f9b3aa8bf944a7feca6948bc9b4f8b714976f2a4f40ee10776f871c3970cd2" "q-335401/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/valid