uid "9ee4b340-1bd0-5b48-9e9c-d93dcfd12d40" :question/math-academy-id "q-335404" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-At}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335404/field-1" "q-335404/field-2" "q-335404/field-3" "q-335404/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-1/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer/id #uuid "5c1e9b32-593c-5578-80f0-5ae1c58ef258" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" :answer/id #uuid "f720135c-48bb-5fe8-a3fa-6ee5eb08243a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-1/3553cedeff4c8d1807c2e5ee6d248ad1263c81ed92e6cc6e85bc709e30fdfbdf" :answer/id #uuid "7ba2e83c-bb5c-55bd-bcc0-0859228cbc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-1/cdbecfab207c35273b9bbf54109508ce15a8f0badaf08aa004621ccb3599529f" :answer/id #uuid "2ffc6b58-41ae-5824-acc1-2df67d390ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c28c8d88-52e0-5