37ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" "q-335420/field-2/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" "q-335420/field-2/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" "q-335420/field-2/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-3/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer/id #uuid "31d3c415-e3ab-5e03-81d5-4318216ae2ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-3/3e795f0a362bd915f79f0cb4de5dd3c4342496d2e05a121a9cad080cf748cbd7" :answer/id #uuid "0151f685-3a64-59de-9f5a-2f79a903eafc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer/id #uuid "00fe2540-d549-5f50-93bf-aa2dd71446f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-3/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143" :answer/id #uuid "1e42b329-756d-5c9b-89ee-20e14ea098ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f29e9d7b-81b4-5e58-93cd-68d137a50098" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335420/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer-field/choices ["q-335420/field-3/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" "q-335420/field-3/3e795f0a362bd915f79f0cb4de5dd3c4342496d2e05a121a9cad080cf748cbd7" "q-335420/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" "q-335420/field-3/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335420" :question/id #uuid "8e9e9aa1-972a-5335-8521-470987b0b354" :question/math-academy-id "q-335420" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335420/field-1" "q-335420/field-2" "q-335420/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335420"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228141 :answer-field/correct 17592186228145 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186229617 :question/answer-fields 17592186228146] {:db/id "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer/id #uuid "0ccf4b39-65d3-57e3-81bd-8bd2157b88a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" :answer/id #uuid "83a4e4ce-ebd7-5315-a33d-f4610afe7777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d" :answer/id #uuid "8702f907-3bd2-5237-81f8-c01695050ba0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960" :answer-field/id #uuid "149e2923-8a99-59cc-a19a-30ed0039af2e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer-field/choices ["q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" "q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960/042168976629a933b0d0ef460bdad0013cb33b8a34cdbca393ce80067da1046d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228136 :answer-field/correct 17592186228138 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228150 :answer-field/correct 17592186228152 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334533"] :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334533/field-2/ma-v1/6ac60219b3fbe1b0bba31091866d2e59c0aff94f4805fb2902723a25183d4960"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-1/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer/id #uuid "4805d631-8043-5bb9-ba6d-3cedb41d8fd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-1/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer/id #uuid "1dc6f512-ef91-5294-b10e-de13b2e7a78b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" :answer/id #uuid "3fc1024f-5c3b-55a0-96ae-91baeaddeaf1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-1/c8c888d652d9e928c6a78739ff870282b257337a10fe3e679e7dccf42d34514b" :answer/id #uuid "15779f5c-5c93-514b-b989-84f0f4721aed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "integrating both sides from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0451cd06-6f05-5d38-baeb-4c3f8cfa38fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335424/field-1/c8c888d652d9e928c6a78739ff870282b257337a10fe3e679e7dccf42d34514b" :answer-field/choices ["q-335424/field-1/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" "q-335424/field-1/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" "q-335424/field-1/18a578c7b04a3b815ae5d4a457af4a650d712815d58e13e1ae858eb82215727e" "q-335424/field-1/c8c888d652d9e928c6a78739ff870282b257337a10fe3e679e7dccf42d34514b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-2/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143" :answer/id #uuid "b64864c3-fc5f-52ee-bbd0-870133e54c4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-2/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" :answer/id #uuid "e5fe0890-622b-5ab2-8f71-bd82269881fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-2/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer/id #uuid "948ae364-9484-56f7-8f22-6cbae081175c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-2/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer/id #uuid "bc242cc7-1f2d-5992-a105-9b9f310cca48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "393742fc-3907-5989-ac64-d52cb29f17c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335424/field-2/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-335424/field-2/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143" "q-335424/field-2/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" "q-335424/field-2/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" "q-335424/field-2/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-3/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143" :answer/id #uuid "cf1db3e9-bb25-5c63-b3fa-2b1c41f2e5fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer/id #uuid "6cc05714-cdfc-59b9-8918-517a992a4338" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-3/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" :answer/id #uuid "6e95564b-e101-5a1a-80e5-68d50de5a61d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-3/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6" :answer/id #uuid "4f6ebe58-36ea-55f4-8f9b-45eb98a5fb8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e61db412-351c-5b86-846a-44c9f9a7a726" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335424/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" :answer-field/choices ["q-335424/field-3/26d127a95d304dbdd7adffc27a42a2c2fd29dd6893f9f60cf304e38ecb659143" "q-335424/field-3/3e398d603a43d67ea0c2e6aaf97b937ceca671994606ecb832c571efa5b91015" "q-335424/field-3/0ba2d57a283410bc2e964e7528110750e41526c5ef29b851dde5d8dd369a44c0" "q-335424/field-3/c19eeb748c0840b522e06ff831279ffd81115e653238a195a6befae39a5135a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335424" :question/id #uuid "8a6363e6-63d5-5501-9372-6389974cbb5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-335424" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$ from ${t}_{0}$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by $\\text{integrating both sides from }{t}_{0}\\text{ to }t.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-335424/field-1" "q-335424/field-2" "q-335424/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21722"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/101a0c499e4eb8557917785388737fb12c85713d204efaad74b13720d53d90a9.png)\nFill in the blanks in the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/b1b5a17a8facd73638545861a9ec05ee2fdebdc2ae8f327fc86f1517085bcd77.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/52808e8499c76638f512feb7dd3721814844cbfb29deb7126ed9e8872a699031.png)*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\, \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/ed2abaaded6d82b6ab9ae856b8f31f99d97bd34515715e36b71d2731049e5e75.png) So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/56f10da4c0759fd5616557c00ce5aa1062190b3fbaaa2ab0dff0d50ef3fb2615.png)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3(t-1){e}^{4(t-1)} \\\\ 3{e}^{4(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21720"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/cf38da5e2aec9fc3957f52abc58fc396686db632561953991a3ca0fc23799ace.png)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/1a1e4510a1ea4961976e22504d6be845edffd972cc88dda0fde4608b50be2b09.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/cfc60391cfb7369d109e7d56b89b6bfd1f97e7251aacb637f61c94d24cdb4f00.png)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/802292289f84a7d69cfaadd91d88d6a4af9560f618dfae6b553fbca16b63cb96.png)\nwhere ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/a851d7868235cdaf8cd6914d21b648b3bd7453549748f4bacc3caf5485c17e50.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/696a10263a0fe8a52e0da4a413956bb4040220de2c22ae41f76032f7045a5265.png) So, the matrix of the system is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/c62e0b111e20b925570d7f178ac556293597b071d9aefb821adc70d83afcb91e.png)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x(t_0)$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/b7b3cf84162533f6b86e3faf8bba17b335ade35acb42d18aa768a5a1db900730.png)\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t = t_0 = 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/5f80485e8a40e46b5c11656dae755f51f7b0617cbe8b4369cf330f329d042283.png)\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-3s+3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/dbce2a7dd9077db8a6e4f85a0b54c9d2563cad3a0ef5a0a98606ca7a4bb5f81f.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21721"] :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}'(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(t)$  \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0) = \\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t)$\n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\displaystyle\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)}\\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s$\n\nFill in the blanks with the correct reasons to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/befe715ac2d9375061b1a3c8c0528a0bfb2764197cee4eca4d2b60146cec20b6.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/09febb48bb00d22caebf088103181b5db6377befccad18f1370718351cc91e9d.png).\n\n$\\quad$ Line $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/999db06dcfe0878ddb3316b11546668ba9442d8fd110165e5076b90964b84905.png)." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L2}$ and $\\textrm{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}'(t) = -Ae^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t) + e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}'(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\textrm{L2}$ and substituting $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\textrm{L3}$ follows from $\\textrm{L2}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/9dcfd90e4444195ee781ab388b36a575ec1219d1820f7141114e29311941ddc5.png)\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Evaluating $\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)$ at $t=t_0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=I\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from line $\\textrm{L1}$  by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/90a07cffb30b2ef860b0d3314865a7bd9ca0b7c86811a63b07628c768188af3e.png)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L1}$ and $\\textrm{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\textrm{L1}$ by $e^{A(t-t_0)}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{L8}$ follows from $\\textrm{L1}$ by ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071250/assets/23a2ac9e75c9bac22187814f524d919166d3748f1caa5831d664231a80bac296.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
